OL,3,GNEWSAMini camera makes bowel cancer
OL,4,Achecks painless
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Kent hospital has begun offering a
OL,7,Fnew and painless method of being
OL,8,Fchecked for symptoms of bowel cancer.
OL,10,FInstead of an uncomfortable and
OL,11,Fintrusive colonoscopy, involving a tube
OL,12,Fbeing inserted into the bowel, patients
OL,13,Fcan now swallow a pill-sized camera
OL,14,Fthat captures images as it passes
OL,15,Fthrough the intestine.
OL,17,FThe first patient to use the technology
OL,18,Fwhen it was launched on 28 October at
OL,19,Fthe Medway Maritime Hospital was
OL,20,F65-year-old Mark Freeman, from
OL,21,FWalderslade.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
